+# ADR-0005: Use AccessKit's C ABI for native Linux accessibility
+
+- Status: accepted in the ak5/symbiote-native fork; implementation in progress
+- Date: 2026-10-30
+
+## Decision
+
+Map the retained native scene to AccessKit through its maintained C bindings.
+Use the Unix adapter's real AT-SPI/D-Bus transport. The host remains C++; Rust is
+a build dependency of the library. React Native, Fabric and Yoga stay unchanged.
+
+Pin accesskit-c 0.23.1 to `e9f6614309eeb820ff03cacd174b1dccee98250c` and
+Corrosion 0.6.1 to `1499b14e4906a2890f5cee1547c8848db261753d`. The C binding's
+committed Cargo.lock selects accesskit 0.25.1 and accesskit_unix 0.24.0. Build
+with `--locked`, at most two Cargo jobs, and Rust 1.87 or newer. Consume the
+published C header and static-library CMake targets.
+
+## Native tree and identity
+
+The frame thread copies semantic nodes, focus, editor selection and transformed
+geometry under one mounting-manager lock. Unpainted accessible views remain in
+this snapshot. Geometry reuses the renderer's transform, scroll and clipping
+calculations. The bridge publishes a complete immutable tree while accessibility
+is active; AccessKit computes platform changes and notifications.
+
+Assign each native Create a monotonically increasing identity. Updates keep it;
+deleting and recreating a Fabric tag gives it a new identity. AccessKit identifiers
+reserve one value for the window and derive native/text-run identifiers from
+that creation identity. A new WindowSession owns a new adapter on reload.
+
+Roles, labels, hints, state, values and labelled-by relations use native props.
+Text-run boundaries follow the editor's ICU graphemes. Password text is masked
+before crossing the C ABI, and field contents do not become an implicit field
+label. Window-relative geometry uses the native content offset. No global
+Wayland window position or glyph metrics are invented.
+
+## Threading and lifetime
+
+The Unix adapter calls activation, action and deactivation handlers on another
+thread. Activation wakes the frame loop through an owned eventfd and returns no
+tree; the frame thread supplies the real full update through AccessKit's documented
+asynchronous activation path. The window polls the borrowed descriptor alongside
+its Wayland connection, including while a compositor withholds frame callbacks.
+
+Actions enter a bounded queue. The frame thread checks the current emitter,
+role and enabled/focusable state before using its native focus and activation
+paths. A recycled or removed control cannot receive an old action. The frame thread
+also rejects a newly hidden target or ancestor, even while the transport still
+holds the previous publication. Worker
+callbacks never call Fabric, Wayland or JSI.
+
+AccessKit's Unix Adapter::drop queues RemoveAdapter asynchronously. Opaque callback
+tokens therefore resolve through weak registrations instead of pointing at a
+WindowSession. Closing removes the registration before freeing the adapter;
+in-flight handlers retain their own state, and later handlers find no session.
+The process-lifetime registration index retains no closed session data.
+
+## Verification and remaining work
+
+Native unit tests must cover geometry, clipping, unpainted nodes, caret/focus
+snapshots, recycling and stale actions. A real AT-SPI client must walk all six
+core components in a running Symbiote app, inspect Unicode and protected text,
+observe focus/caret/state events and activate a native control. Lifecycle races
+need sanitizer checks. Startup or an automation JSON tree alone proves none of
+these transport requirements.
+
+The transport connects focus, activation, editable text and selection to the
+native controller. Edits carry an independent content revision, so controlled
+updates that leave React event counts unchanged still revoke stale requests.
+The controller applies its existing normalization and length limits, emits
+native change events, and rejects writes during composition or to read-only
+fields. Full role-conformance enumeration and precise optional text geometry
+still require their own implementation and checks. AccessKit's uint8 character-length ABI uses a readable label fallback for a
+selectable cluster over 255 UTF-8 bytes; range navigation is unavailable there.
+AccessKit's Label role derives its readable name from `value`; the fallback
+therefore sets the native value, preserving static text without inventing a text
+range. Editable fields keep their own label and expose a readable child value.
+Do not report the accessibility target complete while these checks are pending.
+
+## Sources
+
+- [C bindings and build contract](https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit-c/tree/e9f6614309eeb820ff03cacd174b1dccee98250c)
+- [Activation and text contracts](https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit/blob/accesskit-v0.25.1/accesskit/src/lib.rs)
+- [Consumer label/value contract](https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit/blob/accesskit_unix-v0.24.0/accesskit_consumer/src/node.rs)
+- [Unix adapter lifecycle](https://github.com/AccessKit/accesskit/blob/accesskit_unix-v0.24.0/adapters/unix/src/adapter.rs)
+- [Existing host decision question](https://github.com/react-native-linux/react-native-linux/issues/347)
+
+All implementation and publication remain in the owner's fork. This decision
+does not authorize submissions to another repository.
